on","filename":"48639821922_28c32cbc6e_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/48639821922/","height":2709,"id":"48639821922","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/48639821922/48639821922_28c32cbc6e_o.jpg","sha256":"2f4e9fd31d4a36e6892bcedf1248043dcfc22567bdef45802e2d52da516199f7","tags":["cochem","mosel river","germany","eu"],"taken":"2019-04-21 04:21:51","title":"IMG_1806","uploaded":"2019-08-28 19:25:27","width":4609},"48639822012":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":11838},{"id":"72157710465984236","position":30}],"bytes":2376433,"camera_position":11860,"comments":[{"author":"50167308@N06","date":"2019-08-31 10:58:16","text":"As a motorcyclist I know these warning signs of course. There are some high frequented roads (I call them \"approach air corridors\") where the big crowd of motorcyclists like kind of lemmings get in and out of a certain area. That\u2019s where those signs are mostly positioned at. Often this kind of roads are a pain in the neck for residents living nearby. The protest against motorcyclists is on the rise and ends often enough in road closures.\n\nIn most of the cases I try to avoid these \"lemming routes\", I rather prefer \"B\" and \"C\" category country roads.\n\nIf you love motorcycling yourself, it's a shame to see this passion fall into disrepute because some can't behave."}],"description":"","detail":"photos/0185.json","filename":"48639822012_7442069266_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/48639822012/","height":1863,"id":"48639822012","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/48639822012/48639822012_7442069266_o.jpg","sha256":"39dda6018eda7d3b05ed937b9e0be5f7de6d1bde5f4a8656d770fe8e56a3b307","tags":["cochem","mosel river","germany","eu"],"taken":"2019-04-21 03:44:13","title":"IMG_1803","uploaded":"2019-08-28 19:25:28","width":3885},"48653762548":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":11860},{"id":"721